# Append-only logs. Two loops on two branches append to the same end of each
# of these, so without a union merge every rebase conflicts — which would make
# `design/loops.md` §13's "the rebase is conflict-free by construction" false
# the first time a second loop ran.
#
# Union is correct here rather than merely convenient: every row is a complete
# record carrying its own timestamp, nothing refers to a neighbouring line, and
# duplicate suppression downstream is by id. Order across the seam does not
# matter because nothing reads these positionally.
#
# It is *not* correct for prose — `state/spec-changelog/` is one file per loop
# for that reason, since interleaving two entries line by line yields a third
# entry neither loop wrote.
state/**/*.jsonl merge=union
state/*.jsonl merge=union
